WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:01.420
He's not answering any questions.

00:00:01.540 --> 00:00:01.880
That's okay.

00:00:02.000 --> 00:00:02.600
I have no questions.

00:00:02.880 --> 00:00:03.200
That's right.

00:00:03.520 --> 00:00:04.820
I'm about to monologue, son.

00:00:05.020 --> 00:00:05.720
better make it quick.

00:00:05.960 --> 00:00:06.830
You only got eight minutes.

00:00:06.840 --> 00:00:08.000
All right, then let me paint you a picture.

00:00:08.260 --> 00:00:11.540
of Philip, a successful periodontist that's become addicted to Diazepam,

00:00:11.600 --> 00:00:13.280
a sedative I take because I'm junkie scum.

00:00:13.360 --> 00:00:14.720
Also, for real, addiction is a disease.

00:00:14.720 --> 00:00:16.660
I would be super empathetic if you hadn't murdered a man.

00:00:16.660 --> 00:00:17.510
What is the point of this?

00:00:17.520 --> 00:00:17.980
I'll get there.

00:00:18.040 --> 00:00:20.940
So, one day I'm working late when my boss Robert surprises me.

00:00:21.000 --> 00:00:22.240
He found out I was stealing meds.

00:00:22.260 --> 00:00:23.060
again, junkie scum.

00:00:23.120 --> 00:00:24.100
also again, not your fault.

00:00:24.180 --> 00:00:25.640
There's a major genetic component to addiction.

00:00:25.740 --> 00:00:27.140
He says he's gonna file a police report.

00:00:27.460 --> 00:00:28.440
I could lose my license.

00:00:28.600 --> 00:00:30.200
We fight, and something in me just snaps,

00:00:30.380 --> 00:00:33.010
so I grab the first thing I can find, and I hit him with it.

00:00:33.020 --> 00:00:34.120
You still have no murder weapon.

00:00:34.220 --> 00:00:34.740
I do now.

00:00:35.240 --> 00:00:38.200
Here's a pic I found on Yelp of the surgical suite six months ago,

00:00:38.280 --> 00:00:41.000
and here is a shot that our crime scene photographer took of the same room

00:00:41.000 --> 00:00:41.900
two weeks after the murder.

00:00:42.020 --> 00:00:42.660
Notice any differences?

00:00:42.900 --> 00:00:43.590
We're not answering that.

00:00:43.600 --> 00:00:44.820
That's all right, I can just tell you myself.

00:00:44.820 --> 00:00:48.340
The Yelp shot has six of these heavy looking glass awards from the Brooklyn

00:00:48.340 --> 00:00:50.020
Periodontics Society in the background,

00:00:50.260 --> 00:00:52.080
whereas this shot only has five.

00:00:52.380 --> 00:00:53.320
What happened to number six?

00:00:53.600 --> 00:00:54.670
You Murdered Robert with it!

00:00:54.680 --> 00:00:57.160
You lost all control and you bludgeoned him to death.

00:00:57.280 --> 00:00:59.300
There must have been blood everywhere, but you got lucky.

00:00:59.720 --> 00:01:02.220
You were in the surgical suite; it can be sterilized.

00:01:02.280 --> 00:01:04.140
You never would have gotten away with it in your carpeted office.

00:01:04.300 --> 00:01:04.980
That's not what happened.

00:01:05.020 --> 00:01:05.890
Don't say anything more, Philip.

00:01:05.900 --> 00:01:09.840
And your office manager would have heard all of the screaming but she was at her grandson's play.

00:01:10.220 --> 00:01:10.760
Lucky again.

00:01:10.880 --> 00:01:13.720
You put Robert's body into a wheelchair and shoved it in the elevator.

00:01:13.720 --> 00:01:15.480
It's a miracle there wasn't blood everywhere.

00:01:15.560 --> 00:01:16.300
That's not true.

00:01:16.320 --> 00:01:17.750
Now you're in the garage with a corpse.

00:01:17.760 --> 00:01:21.280
You panicked and left your phone in your office, and you don't have your car keys,

00:01:21.320 --> 00:01:24.620
but Robert's are in his pocket so you put him in his car and you take off.

00:01:24.940 --> 00:01:25.890
You can't believe what you've done.

00:01:25.900 --> 00:01:26.100
No.

00:01:26.380 --> 00:01:26.920
You're flustered.

00:01:26.920 --> 00:01:29.000
You have no GPS, so you just start driving.

00:01:29.120 --> 00:01:29.280
No!
